{
  "title": "iOS UI tests: find what holds test processes before exec during ~5 minute launch hangs",
  "description": "In about 3 of 11 iOS UI runs, a test process launch stalls for 3-5 minutes on an otherwise idle runner. \
The runs usually still pass. \
'Failed to launch com.ramekin.app' in run 37211763439 is probably the same hang running past XCTest's limit. \
Earlier sightings, all inside XCUIApplication.launch(): 37256369854 (185 s), 37252858637 (276 s), 37333289156 (293 s, no Ramekin process until 15:52:21). \
Ruled out: CPU starvation, the 'IDELaunchParametersSnapshot ... no debugger version' lines, relaunch-only effects, building in the same xcodebuild run, and mediaanalysisd. \
Findings from runs 37389551049, 37391591512 and 37392182564, read from simulator-system.log.gz and xcodebuild's session log in the xcresult: (1) The pre-exec stall. \
In 37392182564, xcodebuild launched RamekinUITests-Runner (pid 10393) with activate_suspended=1 at 00:16:27 UTC and logged 'Test process runnable PID is 10393' at 00:16:39. \
Nothing in either log mentions that pid until launchd_sim's '[pid/10393 [RamekinUITests-]:] uncorking exec source upfront' at 00:21:21, 294 s later, while host load fell to about 12. testmanagerd was already up, and xcodebuild was just waiting for the runner to connect. \
The process was stuck between spawn and exec. \
That stage runs in the host's exec and code-signing path (AMFI, syspolicyd, XProtect), which the simulator log cannot show. \
The earlier 293 s app-launch hang ('no Ramekin process until ...') looks like the same thing hitting the app instead of the runner. (2) Slow but non-hanging launches are mostly installs. \
XCTest installs Ramekin.app lazily inside the first launch(). \
That install took 9 s in 37389551049, 35 s in 37392182564 (27 s of it silent between CoreSimulatorBridge's 'Request received for installation' and installcoordinationd registering the placeholder), and 63 s in 37391591512. \
In 37391591512 the runner install also took over 2 minutes, at host load 100-570 during the simulator boot storm. \
Pre-installing with simctl probably would not help, because xcodebuild reinstalls on first launch. \
The CI job now also uploads logs/host-exec.log.gz: the host's log for amfid, syspolicyd, XprotectService, CoreSimulatorService, and AMFI/codesign/xpcproxy_sim kernel lines. \
Next step: find a run where a launch stalls over 60 s between xcodebuild's 'Launched app ... (pid = N)' or 'Test process runnable PID is N' and launchd_sim's '[pid/N ...] uncorking exec source upfront'. \
Then read host-exec.log.gz for that window and pick a targeted fix. \
If the host log is silent too, widen its predicate. \
To get xcodebuild's session log from the xcresult without macOS: zstd -dc each ios-ui-tests.xcresult/Data/data.* blob and grep for 'Test process runnable'. \
To get timings from the job log: grep 'Launch com.ramekin.app' and 'Setting up automation session'. \
This hang also undermines the keyboard warm-up (KeyboardWarmupTests, make ios-warm-ui-keyboard). \
That warm-up keeps the simulator keyboard process (InputUI) from cold-launching mid-test, which once stalled the app's main thread for minutes ('process main thread busy for 30.0s', run 37389551049). \
Across runs from 2026-10-07 to 2026-10-09, no stall followed a warm launch. \
But the warm-up failed in 3 of 10 runs (37644698155, 37699386596, 37945361291), each time because the app never became snapshot-able after launch. \
In those runs InputUI cold-launched in testLoginFailure again, with short keyboard-queue timeouts. \
The warm-up now retries once and posts a CI warning annotation if it still fails, so watch for that annotation. \
The hang is not limited to the first launch: in 37954090122, testLoginFailure spent 5 minutes on 'App event loop idle notification not received' after a successful warm-up.",
